# w.lang.en/shards/pronouns: personal, possessive and demonstrative pronouns (what each refers to: `refers=thing` stands for an item of the scene or the dialogue focus, m/f/any an agent, user/assistant the speaker or the listener), and the
# anaphoric noun phrases of the dialogue ("that one", "this animal"; `order` is the order the dialogue module tries them, longest first). `in=` names the PSys2 view that uses the word.
# sources: PSys2 (hand-written): worlds/acts, dialogue.mjs, continuation.mjs, discourse.mjs, astra/focus.mjs, formalizer/rules/session.mjs
# license: CC0-1.0

@lang.en.pron.it lang.en.pron text=it case=subject,object person=3 number=sg gender=n refers=thing in=acts in=dialogue in=continuation in=astra in=matcher core.source="psys2 closed-class sets 2026-11-14"
